{"version":"https://schema.openattestation.com/3.0/schema.json","network":{"chain":"ASTRON","chainId":"1338"},"credentialSubject":{"etd_type":"Ocean BOL","etd_bl_type":"To Order","etd_reference_number":"XMMX51023700","etd_model_terms":{"etd_notice":"<meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><style> .notice-box { padding: 20px; } .notice-box h2 { font-family: 'Avenir', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 14px; color: #60636B; margin-bottom: 10px; } .notice-box ol { padding-left: 20px; } .notice-box li { font-family: 'Avenir', sans-serif; font-weight: 500; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; letter-spacing: 0; color: #60636B; margin-bottom: 10px; text-align: justify; } .underline-text {border-bottom: 1px solid #60636B;} .custom-ol { counter-reset: custom-counter var(--start, 1); } .custom-ol li { list-style: none; counter-increment: custom-counter; position: relative; padding-left: 25px; } .custom-ol li::before { content: counter(custom-counter) \". \"; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; line-height: 1.5; vertical-align: middle; } .custom-ol { --start: attr(data-start number); } </style><div class=\"notice-box clause-section\"><h2><span>A. <span class=\"underline-text\">Notice</span></span></h2><ol class=\"custom-ol\" style=\"--start: 0;\" data-start=\"0\"><li> This is a SGTraDex TradeTrust (&ldquo;TT&rdquo;) electronic bill of lading (&ldquo;eBL&rdquo;) governed by the laws of <span id=\"governingLaw\" class=\"replaceable\">Singapore</span> which has adopted the United Nations Commission on International Trade Law (&ldquo;UNCITRAL&rdquo;) Model Law on Electronic Transferable Records (&ldquo;MLETR&rdquo;). This TT eBL meets the requirements of the MLETR as implemented under <span id=\"governingLaw\" class=\"replaceable\">Singapore</span> law which gives legal recognition to it as equivalent to a paper bill of lading. </li><li> In the event of any conflict or inconsistency between this SGTraDex TT eBL Additional Terms and Conditions (&ldquo;Additional Terms and Conditions&rdquo;) and the terms and conditions of the standard form charterparties or bills of lading on liner terms, the terms and conditions of this TT eBL Terms and Conditions shall prevail to the extent of the conflict or inconsistency. </li></ol></div>","etd_model_terms":"<meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><style>  .model-terms {    padding: 20px;  }  .model-terms h2 {    font-family: 'Avenir', sans-serif;    font-weight: 500;    font-size: 14px;    color: #60636B;    margin-bottom: 10px;  }  .model-terms .heading-text {    line-height: 1.5;    text-decoration: underline;  }  .model-terms ol {    padding-left: 18px;    list-style-position: outside;  }  .model-terms li {    padding-left: 0px;    margin-left: -3px;    font-family: 'Avenir', sans-serif;    font-weight: 500;    font-size: 14px;    line-height: 1.5;    letter-spacing: 0;    color: #60636B;    margin-bottom: 10px;    text-align: justify;  }  .model-terms li:has(ol) {    text-align: left;  }  .model-terms li p.subtext {    padding-left: 20px;    margin-top: 10px;    font-size: 14px;  }  .replaceable {    display: inline-block;    position: relative;  }  .underline-text {border-bottom: 1px solid #60636B;}  ol.alpha-paren {    list-style: none;    counter-reset: alpha-counter;    padding-left: 20px;  }  ol.alpha-paren>li {    counter-increment: alpha-counter;    position: relative;    padding-left: 25px;    margin-bottom: 10px;  }  ol.alpha-paren>li::before {    content: \"(\" counter(alpha-counter, lower-alpha) \") \";    position: absolute;    left: 0;    color: #60636B;  }  .custom-ol {    counter-reset: custom-counter var(--start, 1);  }  .custom-ol li {    list-style: none;    counter-increment: custom-counter;    position: relative;    padding-left: 25px;  }  .custom-ol li::before {    content: counter(custom-counter) \". \";    position: absolute;    left: 0;    top: 0;    line-height: 1.5;    vertical-align: middle;  }  .custom-ol {    --start: attr(data-start number);  }</style><div class=\"model-terms clause-section\"><h2><span>B. <span class=\"underline-text\">Carrier's Right to Receive Back</span></span></h2><ol class=\"custom-ol\" style=\"--start: 2;\" data-start=\"2\"><li> This TT eBL has been issued and/or signed by the Carrier using the SGTraDex system. The Carrier has the right to receive this TradeTrust eBL back on the SGTraDex system from which it issued and/or signed when the TradeTrust eBL is surrendered in return for discharge of the cargo as further set out below. </li></ol><h2><span>C. <span class=\"underline-text\">Switch to Paper</span></span></h2><ol class=\"custom-ol\" style=\"--start: 3;\" data-start=\"3\"><li> At any time prior to the delivery of the goods covered by the TT eBL, the Carrier undertakes, at the request of any lawful holder of the TT eBL, to accept the return by way of transfer of possession of the TT eBL and issue a paper bill of lading in its place. Upon acceptance of the return of the TT eBL, the TT eBL shall be made inoperative and ceases to have any effect or validity and no further transfer of possession of the TT eBL shall be permitted. The paper bill of lading shall accurately reflect the wording of the TT eBL together with the terms and conditions contained in and/or incorporated by reference in the TT eBL. The change of medium in accordance with this clause C.4 shall not affect the rights and obligations of the parties. The paper bill of lading shall state the date of issue in accordance with the TT eBL, the date of conversion to paper and the paper bill of lading shall be accompanied by a printout of the electronic record of holders between the date of issue and the date of conversion to paper. </li><li> The paper bill of lading issued in place of the TT eBL shall contain the following statement: <p class=\"subtext\"> \"This is a paper bill of lading issued and signed by the Carrier in compliance with a request from the lawful holder of the TradeTrust eBL on [date of request to switch to paper] to switch to paper. Pursuant to the governing law of <span id=\"governingLaw\" class=\"replaceable\">Singapore</span>, being an MLETR-compliant jurisdiction, the change of medium shall not affect the rights and obligations of the parties. The TradeTrust eBL has been made inoperative and has ceased to have any effect or validity and no further endorsement or transfer of possession of the eBL shall be permitted.\" </p></li></ol><h2><span>D. <span class=\"underline-text\">Surrender, Delivery and Accomplishment</span></span></h2><ol class=\"custom-ol\" style=\"--start: 5;\" data-start=\"5\"><li> Upon acceptance of the surrender of the TT eBL, the Carrier shall be entitled to require reasonable proof of identity from the party taking delivery of the <span id=\"deliveryOrderOption\" class=\"replaceable\">goods or receiving the Delivery Order and</span> thereafter, subject to any legal exception or impediment to its obligation, to deliver the cargo to the party entitled to take delivery. Upon making delivery of the goods in this clause D.6, the TT eBL shall be made inoperative and ceases to have any effect or validity in transferring title and no further transfer of possession of the TT eBL shall be permitted. The Carrier shall then record the status of the TT eBL as accomplished. </li></ol><h2><span>E. <span class=\"underline-text\">Governing Law and Dispute Resolution</span></span></h2><ol class=\"custom-ol\" style=\"--start: 6;\" data-start=\"6\"><li> These Additional Terms and Conditions shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of <span id=\"governingLaw\" class=\"replaceable\">Singapore</span>. </li><li> Any dispute arising out of or in connection with these Additional Terms and Conditions, including any question regarding the TT eBL's existence, validity or termination, shall be referred to and finally resolved by arbitration administered by the <span id=\"disputeResolutionCentre\" class=\"replaceable\">SCMA Rules (Singapore Chamber of Maritime Arbitration)</span> in accordance with the Arbitration Rules of the <span id=\"disputeResolutionCentre\" class=\"replaceable\">SCMA Rules (Singapore Chamber of Maritime Arbitration)</span> current at the commencement of the arbitration, which rules are deemed to be incorporated by reference in this clause E.8. <ol class=\"alpha-paren\"><li>The seat of the arbitration shall be <span id=\"arbitrationSeat\" class=\"replaceable\">Singapore</span>.</li><li>The tribunal shall consist of <span id=\"numberOfArbitrators\" class=\"replaceable\">three</span> arbitrator(s).</li><li>The language of the arbitration shall be in English.</li><li>The law governing this arbitration agreement shall be <span id=\"governingLaw\" class=\"replaceable\">Singapore</span> law.</li></ol></li></ol></div>"},"etd_transport_doc_pdf":{"attachments":[{"filename":"XMMX51023700.pdf","file_content":""}]}},"@context":["https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1","https://schemata.openattestation.com/com/openattestation/1.0/OpenAttestation.v3.json","https://schema.dev.sgtradex.io/io/sgtradex/external_transport_document/1.0/external_transport_document-context.json"],"issuanceDate":"2025-10-29T09:13:37.507Z","openAttestationMetadata":{"template":{"name":"EXTERNAL_TRANSPORT_DOCUMENT","type":"EMBEDDED_RENDERER","url":"https://renderer.sgtradex.io/?logoID=undefined"},"proof":{"type":"OpenAttestationProofMethod","method":"TOKEN_REGISTRY","value":"0xF047C1227A99dC6ff40a809e9d921379BEde7C59","revocation":{"type":"NONE"}},"identityProof":{"type":"DNS-TXT","identifier":"verifier-astron-l2.pil-pitstop-ucg.pitstop.sgtradex.io"}},"issuer":{"id":"https://pil-pitstop-ucg.pitstop.sgtradex.io","name":"Pacific International Lines Pte Ltd","type":"OpenAttestationIssuer"},"type":["VerifiableCredential","OpenAttestationCredential"],"proof":{"type":"OpenAttestationMerkleProofSignature2018","proofPurpose":"assertionMethod","targetHash":"ee1b120b298115ef00fa2969ec44f065f2cde32f2f5689abc02cf5d4d1a0e57f","proofs":[],"merkleRoot":"ee1b120b298115ef00fa2969ec44f065f2cde32f2f5689abc02cf5d4d1a0e57f","salts":"","privacy":{"obfuscated":[]}},"id":"urn:uuid:fbf9adea-01c9-4dbe-b81a-846d2fd0fbd9","attachments":[]}